= Tool use (artificial intelligence) — Technical =

== Tool interface ==
A tool can be represented by a callable interface:

<pre>
τ : input schema → execution result
</pre>

A tool-using policy chooses whether to invoke τ, which tool to choose, and how to construct valid arguments.

== Stages ==
Modern tool-learning systems often separate:

<pre>
tool retrieval
tool selection
argument generation
execution
observation parsing
result integration
multi-tool planning/orchestration
</pre>

Different systems learn or hand-code different stages.

== Long-horizon orchestration ==
Long trajectories introduce state dependence, error propagation, cost, latency, safety constraints, and partial observability.

Multi-tool orchestration is therefore more than repeated independent function calls.

